 about Heberden's nodes.\n\n  Which of the following statements suits best with this extract?\n\n  A. Abnormal growth of bones on finger joints is called interphalangeal joints.\n\n  B. Cartilage layer causes the bones to damage gradually over time.\n\n  C. Osteoarthritis is not the only cause for Heberden’s nodes.", "sourcePage": 41, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 48, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 27, "prompt": "You hear a discussion between a nurse and a physician explaining about\nsurgical treatments for patients with a desiccated disc.\n\nThe extra bone that has moved out of place is removed in;\n\nA. Fusion method\n\nB. Correction method\n\nC. Decompression method", "sourcePage": 42, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 48, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 28, "prompt": "You hear a discussion between a nurse and a physician explaining about\noutcomes of TB skin test.\n\nWhich of the following statements is correct?\n\nA. Patients vaccinated using the bacillus Calmette-Guérin show a positive result for TB\n\nB. Patients exposed measles show a false negative result to TB\n\nC. If the bump is larger than 5 millimeters then the test result is considered negative for TB", "sourcePage": 42, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 48, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 29, "prompt": "You hear a discussion between a nurse and a physician explaining about\n  atelectasis.\n\n  Which of the following statements suits best with this extract?\n\n  A. Alveoli in the lower lobes of the lungs deflate during bibasilar atelectasis.\n\n  B. Bibasilar atelectasis is a partial collapse of lungs\n\n  C. Deflation of alveoli in the lower lobes of the lungs is called atelectasis.", "sourcePage": 43, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 48, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 30, "prompt": "You hear a discussion between a nurse and a physician explaining about\n  liver flukes.\n\n  Which of the following statements is incorrect?\n\n  A. It is difficult to diagnose liver flukes as the symptoms are similar to many other conditions.\n\n  B. Liver flukes is the disease caused by fascioliasis.\n\n  C. Pain in upper right abdomen is caused when liver flukes burrow through the lining of the\n  liver.\n\n\n\n                                                    Part C\n\n       In this part of the test, you'll hear two different extracts. In each extract, you'll hear health\n       professionals talking about specific aspects of their work.\n\n       For questions, 31 to 42 choose the answer (A, B, or C) which fits best according to what you\n       hear. Complete the answers as you listen the audio.\n\n       Now, look at extract one.", "sourcePage": 43, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 48, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}], "skills": ["listening"], "recordings": ["c7ceac3d06755e9fa2659babda5121f73fddfb860afda73ac7d29fe73f588ffd"], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [48]}], "matchEvidence": "Reviewed patient cases and question topics in the exact-recording transcript against the printed task paper; task filename alone is not used"}, {"id": "british-academy-task-4-C", "label": "British Academy · Task 4 · Part C", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "pages": [44, 45, 46, 47], "questions": [{"number": 31, "prompt": "Which of the following statements is incorrect?\n\n       A. Cystic hygroma in embryo can result in miscarriage\n\n       B. Cystic hygroma that are present at the time of birth are malignant\n\n       C. Blockage in the lymphatic system causes cystic hygroma", "sourcePage": 44, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 48, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 32, "prompt": "Which of the following statements is incorrect?\n\n       A. Adult onset cystic hygroma is very rare\n\n       B. 50 percent of the cases of cystic hygroma are due to viral infections to a fetus\n\n       C. Drug and alcohol consumption during pregnancy can also cause cystic hygroma formation", "sourcePage": 44, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 48, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 33, "prompt": "Additional set of chromosomes to the fetus are developed when;\n\nA. The woman misses X chromosome completely or partially\n\nB. There is a Noonan syndrome\n\nC. There is a condition of Trisomy 13, 18 or 21", "sourcePage": 45, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 48, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 34, "prompt": "Unusual facial feature is formed when;\n\nA. There is a Noonan syndrome\n\nB. The woman misses X chromosome completely or partially\n\nC. There is a condition of Trisomy 13, 18 or 21", "sourcePage": 45, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 48, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 35, "prompt": "Which of the following statements is incorrect?\n\nA. Low levels of alpha-fetoproteins is an indication of cystic hygroma\n\nB. Usually cystic hygroma is diagnosed during pregnancy.\n\nC. Blood tests at 15 to 20 weeks of pregnancy can detect cystic hygroma formation", "sourcePage": 45, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": 